ard alone.\n- No focus traps remain in any modal or dialog within the audited flows; focus is restored to the triggering control when a modal closes.\n- Every interactive control in the audited flows is reachable and operable by keyboard.\n- Focus indicators are visually consistent across all interactive controls in the audited flows.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is resolved, or explicitly dispositioned with a recorded reason if out of scope.\n- Automated tests covering keyboard-only completion of the four flows pass in the Dashboard's test suite where such coverage is practical.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the keyboard-operability remediation in this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows — covered by the focus-indicator consistency work in this epic. Bundled with HLR-1: both requirements edit the same modals, focus-management code, and flow surfaces in the same component and team; splitting them would double-touch the same call sites.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24782,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa95b3aa947456a1","agent_id":"a9be80e79a58d55e6","session_id":"0d8c28b9-8702-4bae-9684-c8dd1bf6fab6","uuid":"c1517c3b-d8c3-4b02-9b66-9c6657d668fc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:54:35.910Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
