{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90d41af9ca19d28f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard-accessibility defects identified by the accessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows — project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — so that each flow is fully operable by keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and consistent visible focus indicators.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Resolve every keyboard-operability defect enumerated in the audit report for the four audited flows: focus must be managed correctly when modals and dialogs open and close (focus moved into the dialog on open, restored to the triggering control on close), no focus traps, and no controls unreachable via keyboard navigation.\n38\t- Apply consistent visible focus indicators across all interactive controls in the four audited flows, replacing the inconsistent indicator styling the audit identified.\n39\t- Keyboard operability and focus-indicator consistency are delivered as one pass over the same flows and the same modal/focus-management code; they are not separately schedulable and are bundled in this epic.\n40\t- Where practical, extend the Dashboard's existing automated tests to cover keyboard-only completion of the audited flows so the fixes are regression-protected.\n41\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using the keyboard alone.\n46\t- No focus traps remain in any modal or dialog within the audited flows; focus is restored to the triggering control when a modal closes.\n47\t- Every interactive control in the audited flows is reachable and operable by keyboard.\n48\t- Focus indicators are visually consistent across all interactive controls in the audited flows.\n49\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is resolved, or explicitly dispositioned with a recorded reason if out of scope.\n50\t- Automated tests covering keyboard-only completion of the four flows pass in the Dashboard's test suite where such coverage is practical.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the keyboard-operability remediation in this epic.\n55\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows — covered by the focus-indicator consistency work in this epic. Bundled with HLR-1: both requirements edit the same modals, focus-management code, and flow surfaces in the same component and team; splitting them would double-touch the same call sites.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adfc973ac0df88e6","agent_id":"a34c2622a3adb8ce8","session_id":"0d8c28b9-8702-4bae-9684-c8dd1bf6fab6","uuid":"c0e0710a-0bf1-446d-aa19-b4a94e50f14d","time