mes no owning team for documentation. Verify team assignment before submission.\n57\t- **E001 size / re-split trigger**: the keyboard-accessibility remediation epic bundles keyboard operability for the four audited flows, focus-indicator consistency, and test-extension coverage into one epic that sits at or near the ~2-week guideline. This is one logical pass over one surface (the Dashboard modal and focus-management code shared by the four flows) by one team, so it is not split now; a split would double-touch the same call sites. **Re-split trigger**: if the audit defect count across the four flows exceeds a sprint of Dashboard remediation effort, split the epic along per-flow lines (one epic per audited flow: project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission), each carrying its portion of the HLR-1/HLR-2 scope and acceptance criteria.\n58\t- **No priority inversions detected**: HLR-1/HLR-2 are P1 code fixes; HLR-3 is P2 documentation, correctly sequenced after the fixes it describes.\n59\t- **No scope traps detected**: out-of-scope items (screen-reader semantics beyond keyboard fixes, flows outside the four audited ones) do not contradict any requirement.\n60\t\n61\t## Tiered Delivery\n62\t\n63\tNot applicable — there are no external dependencies with uncertain timing. The two epics run strictly serially (code fixes, then documentation of the fixed state).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87f6cd2186fea345","agent_id":"a19cd0fe87b0ae337","session_id":"0d8c28b9-8702-4bae-9684-c8dd1bf6fab6","uuid":"e9cbb0c7-b199-4dce-9255-5179ef062a00","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:59:48.171Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b31ef9f903939a6a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
